From b8bac29340227694deaf60abedb84b77c8c6b9e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:06:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Amiga: do not expand options as file patterns

With EXPAND_WILDCARDS every argument went through MatchFirst, options
included. An option with a path in it, as "--list=T:names", was taken for
a file on a volume named "--list=T", and DOS asked for that volume to be
inserted. Arguments that start with "-" are now passed on unchanged.

Repository: lha (https://github.com/sodero/lha.git)
Base: 1e7c8f1fc1bd0f72610ca381e21bbda9325cd4f5
Requires: 0001-Amiga-no-UNIX-permission-headers-beside-the-protecti.patch, 0002-Amiga-no-trailing-NUL-in-the-name-when-there-is-no-c.patch, 0003-Add-list-FILE-archive-and-file-names-from-a-file.patch, 0004-Amiga-stop-on-Ctrl-C-while-compressing-without-a-par.patch
Scope: Amiga builds (_AMIGA)
Tested: AROS One 1.3, ABIv11 x86_64 (2026-10-18): a 1229-entry Amiga tree packed and read back identically by Unarc (XAD), and by C:lha except comments, which it does not set; Amiga LhA 2.15, LHa for UNIX and 7-Zip test it OK
Upstream-Status: candidate (not submitted)
Removal: when sodero/lha carries an equivalent change and the pin moves past it
---
 src/lharc.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/lharc.c b/src/lharc.c
index dd60db7..dc1169a 100755
--- a/src/lharc.c
+++ b/src/lharc.c
@@ -803,7 +803,24 @@ expand_argv(int argc, char *argv[], int *argc_x)
     for(int i = 0; i < argc; ++i)
     {
         size_t len = strlen(argv[i]);
-        int err = MatchFirst(argv[i], anchor);
+        int err;
+
+        /* Options are not file patterns: "--list=T:x" would make DOS ask
+           for a volume named "--list=T". */
+        if (i > 0 && argv[i][0] == '-')
+        {
+            argv_x = append_arg(argv_x, &argv_z, argv[i], *argc_x);
+
+            if(!argv_x)
+            {
+                return NULL;
+            }
+
+            ++(*argc_x);
+            continue;
+        }
+
+        err = MatchFirst(argv[i], anchor);
 
         if (err || (len && argv[i][len - 1] == '/' &&
             strncmp(argv[i], anchor->ap_Buf, len - 1) == 0))
